      "message": "We talked about being able to set some of the bits of the BoardID.Flags very early in the factory, most notably the board phase (bits 0-6) and the pre-MP bit (bit 7). This allows to mark devices that don\u0027t have a brand code in pre-MP and quickly get them out of ZT eligibility. See comment about that in go/zte-floors.\n\nI suggest that the test here is limited to checking that BoardID.Type  (and maybe BoardID.Type_Inverted if you want as here) hasn\u0027t been written but leave BoardID.Flags out of this so we have that flexibility later.\n\nWe\u0027ll need a corresponding change in the bid command to allow writing type/type_inverted even after flags have been written.",
